       Many routines return an error code. The value 0 (zero) denotes no error
       happened.  Other  values can be passed to uubb__ssttrreerrrroorr to obtain a read‐
       able error string.   uubb__ssttrreerrrroorr  returns  a  zero  terminated  string.
       uubb__ccttxx__ccrreeaattee returns NULL on an error (a malloc failure).  uubb__ppoollll re‐
       turns  true  if  some  information  may  be available, false otherwise.
       uubb__ffdd returns a file descriptor or  -1  on  error.   uubb__ccttxx__ccoonnffiigg  and
       uubb__ccttxx__rreessoollvvccoonnff  attempt to leave errno informative on a function re‐
       turn with file read failure.

